    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Darlington’s Greersburg Academy, founded by Reverend Thomas Hughes in 1802, still stands as a historic landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.darlingtontwp.com/historical-pictures"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The same Greersburg Academy building once doubled as a railway station for several lines between 1883 and 1972.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.darlingtontwp.com/historical-pictures"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Darlington was first incorporated in 1820 as Greersburg, then renamed in 1830 to avoid confusion with Greensburg, Westmoreland County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darlington%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1800s, Darlington served as a key relay station for stage coaches traveling between Pittsburgh and Cleveland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://bcpahistory.org/beavercounty/BeaverCountyCommunities/darlington/DarlingtonBorough.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The borough is completely surrounded by Darlington Township, making it an enclave within the township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darlington%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A fire in 1925 destroyed the historic Hotel Darlington, the third time the popular hostelry had burned over a century.",
